{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1518764-would-like-inspiration-and-advices-for-interesting-spirit-npcs","id":1518764,"title":"Would like inspiration and advices for interesting Spirit npcs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-25T09:35:14-07:00","id":1518764,"title":"Would like inspiration and advices for interesting Spirit npcs","content":"Soooo, I have been trying to get my players in the Spirit World lately. Here's an issue though: I find it somewhat difficult to picture myself what Spirits look like, let alone design interesting ones. Whenever I try, they tend to come out a bit too much as random mindless monsters for my tastes. I find it relatively easy to design Fae and Hobgoblins (taking inspirations from fairy tales or Celtic Folklore), God-Machine Angels (inspiration from Angels + cyberpunk vibe), but for some reason I am never quite sure what to go for with Spirits, be it on how to roleplay them or how to picture/design them. Anyone could provide me with advices, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T12:12:35-07:00","id":1518773,"title":"","content":"Random monsters is exactly what the spirit world would look like to a human. Maybe one spirit of jealousy looks like a floating green eye ball while the next one looks like a being comprised of nothing but hands all trying to grab at everything in reach. You could have a spirit of sadness that looks like tears flowing down invisible cheeks accompanied by the sounds of weeping. They can really be anything, and their &quot;physical&quot; forms don't matter, at all. <br /> <br /> Spirits of things may resemble twisted, predatory forms of the things they are. Hunting cat cars, buildings with mouths for door ways, birds with camera heads for surveillance systems, anything is possible. <br /> <br /> IMO what matters more in the Shadow is the way it feels. Spirits are hungry. A spirit of sadness, they want more sadness, need it in fact, because their eternal existence literally depends on it. If it's source of sadness dries up it has to find another one, and quick, or feed on something else and risk becoming a magath. <br /> <br /> Also, spirits literally can't do stuff for free. Not &quot;won't&quot; but &quot;can't&quot; in the same way a human &quot;can't&quot; flap their arms to fly, it just doesn't work. You want a spirit to do something for you, you're going to have to pay up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T22:37:03-07:00","id":1518813,"title":"","content":"1. The thing is the thing. Most spirits at least start out resembling their material basis, and spirits of abstract concepts are explicitly less common than more concrete things like cats or fire or airplanes. Most spirits do not eat other spirits who are not at least conceptually related to their own nature without aberrant circumstances, and the vast majority of spirits' Essence intake comes from eating other spirits, so the symbolic language of a spirit's appearance and personality tend to be consistent with its original and/or change very gradually outside of those aberrant circumstances. The complexity of a spirit's form and name scales with its Rank (as does the likelihood that it will not be a pure expression of a singular concept), so Hursihim looking like little more than shadowy forms of their material basis is not uncommon and it'd be a rare sort of Dihir who isn't at least highly detailed. Above all, spirits are what they eat and the things they eat tend to be appropriate to their environments and/or origins \u2014 as the classic example goes, fox-spirits in the urban Shadow look different from fox-spirits from the countryside, and that's mostly from finding things aligned with foxness in those locales and incorporating them into their nature.<br /> <br /> 2. The way the Gauntlet bunches up means things from the Shadow around a collective human presence will tend to be more abstracted from their material basis, whereas out in the wild the landscape tends to limit its divergences to matters of scale. The spirits of plants and animals are more likely to look like plants and animals, whereas the spirits of trains and houses may represent themselves with symbolic anatomy not found in the mortal schematics of these things. Coupled with the lack of direct human spiritual representation, this means spirits with a humanoid body plan are bound to look at least a little bit off.<br /> <br /> 3. Despite the &quot;ephemeral&quot; moniker, the Shadow is made of concrete actors who, lack of disruptable organs notwithstanding, are basically made of an alien type of flesh. Whether a spirit has a body of meat or metal or vapor, it is a present living creature in an ecology where it represents the needs and wants and tendencies of the thing it represents. It does the things it does, and the ability to bargain with it for some amount of payment does little to alter the fact that fire wants to burn, misery loves company, and plants need watering, even if the relationships between these things is a matter of ancient agreement between powerful spirits. Most Essence in the Shadow changing hands from taking the actual lifeblood of immortal prey paints a specific sort of visual with or without a direct comparison to Vampire. Spirits go where they go and do what they do for particular reasons, and knowing what those reasons are is vitally important when dealing with a part of the setting where interconnected actors and knock-on consequences are major thematic elements.<br /> <br /> 4. This also means that most of the common spirits of Rank 2 and below act about how you'd expect something whose continued activity is dependent upon there continuing to be a tree in the park or a beloved car maintained would act. Their expressible desires tend to be unambitious, given the ease with which their bans and banes can disrupt them, so their priorities are liable to be biased toward surviving long enough to rise in Rank over grander schemes.<br /> <br /> 5. Most of spirit politics takes place at Rank 3 and 4, where the spirit has generally outgrown or outlasted the thing that created it and started branching out into related resonance profiles. They're joining descants and engaging in schemes that might bring them across the Gauntlet and otherwise acting like otherworldly versions of player supernatural societies might instead of simply serving as conversational scenery reflecting the activities of the material world. These folks have an interest in secret places, bodies of labor, and other politically useful tools that will allow them to advance their importance among the spirits around them.<br /> <br /> 6. Rank 5 and 6 spirits tend to inhabit secure enough placement in their domains to loop back around to being sources of background noise, because they've built their machines such that their livelihoods depend less on getting a big scheme to go through and more on making sure the old agreements are kept to in the big chaotic mess of interactions between nightfall and streetlamps or winter and spring or sheep and wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-06-2023, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T06:55:07-07:00","id":1523493,"title":"","content":"Alright so based on some of the advices given here, I tried coming up with ideas for designs that Spirits might have (mostly ones of emotions and abstacts concepts, since these seem to be the ones I have the most trouble with). Please do give me Feedback:<br /> <br /> * <b>Knowledge Spirits:</b> living books flying around like birds; living letters and numbers crawling around like insects, being preyed on by the aforementioned books; humanoid figures with robes made of scrolls or maps; a being made of informatic datas;<br /> <br /> * <b>Joy/Fun Spirits:</b> living guitars; clown/mime-like figures with masks showing a smiling laughing face; a floating mouth that seems to be permanently smiling; lightbugs made of fireworks; cotton candy elementals;<br /> <br /> <b>* Anger Spirits:</b> Living signposts with angry faces on them; a monstrous, berserk-like humanoid vaguely looking like a rioter; a being made entirely of mouth that constantly are yelling in angers all in unison;<br /> <br /> <b>* Lust/Desire Spirits:</b> a living heart-shaped figure; a cherub; a living padlock with a heart on it; a living ruban that tries wrapping around people to connect them together; a pink flame elemental;<br /> <br /> <b>* Tourism/Sightseeing Spirit:</b> Living cameras; a pile of souvenir keychains forming a humanoid figure; a pack of eyes that seems to look around constantly in curiosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T08:04:34-07:00","id":1523496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1518764-would-like-inspiration-and-advices-for-interesting-spirit-npcs?p=1523493#post1523493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">;<br /> <b>* Lust/Desire Spirits:</b> a living heart-shaped figure; a cherub; a living padlock with a heart on it; a living <b>ruban</b> that tries wrapping around people to connect them together; a pink flame elemental;[</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you meant &quot;ribbon&quot;, but a lust Spirit that looks like bread made me giggle.<br /> <br /> Edit: ah, what I was thinking of is spelled &quot;reuben&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-03-2023, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T08:37:11-07:00","id":1523499,"title":"","content":"... I did mean ribbon yes^^' Ruban is the french word for it. Though yeah the idea IS pretty funny^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T21:31:11-07:00","id":1523594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1518764-would-like-inspiration-and-advices-for-interesting-spirit-npcs?p=1523496#post1523496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume you meant &quot;ribbon&quot;, but a lust Spirit that looks like bread made me giggle.<br /> <br /> Edit: ah, what I was thinking of is spelled &quot;reuben&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The magath known as <b>Scrumptious Meat</b> has no idea how it came to be. All it remembers is the gnashing of teeth, the sweet smell of young flesh, the softness of fresh bread, and a mind-searing <i>need</i>. It is technically a spirit of hunger, both the actual hunger for good eating and the metaphorical hunger for sensual intimacy, but something in its Essence snapped and failed to reconcile the two concepts.<br /> <br /> The spirit moves frantically about, at one moment trying to make someone eat much more than they normally do, and at another trying to urge someone into making romantic or sexual moves towards any nearby person. Sometimes it does those two things consecutively, causing much confusion. So far the spirit has not thought of inciting the two drives <i>simultaneously</i>, much to everybody's relief.<br /> <br /> Scrumptious Meat appears as, quite awkwardly, a giant Reuben sandwich floating in the air. When it speaks, the bread slices appear as a mouth and lips, with the meat fillings appearing as the tongue and gum and other pieces of flesh in the mouth. The meat filling is notable for looking uncannily attractive, unnervingly resembling the texture of human 'skin' and flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b>: 2 (Spirit)<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 15<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Power 3, Finesse 3, Resistance 4<br /> <b>Size</b>: 2<br /> <b>Corpus</b>: 6<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 7<br /> <b>Initiative</b>: +7<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 3<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 6 (species factor 0)<br /> <br /> <b>Ban</b>: Scrumptious Meat cannot harm or use its Numina and Influences against the express permission of someone who has eaten in the last hour.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane</b>: (no idea; something about lust i suppose)<br /> <br /> <b>Influences</b>: Lust \u2022, Appetite \u2022<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Discorporate, Fetter<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Drain, Emotional Aura (Hunger), Seek, Sign","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T21:45:13-07:00","id":1523598,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Are you proud of yourself? Are you happy with what you have wrought? with the <i>sin</i> you have <i>committed here</i> in front of <i>witnesses</i>?<br /> <br /> If not, why aren't you, this was fucking hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T22:19:13-07:00","id":1523601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1518764-would-like-inspiration-and-advices-for-interesting-spirit-npcs?p=1523594#post1523594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bane</b>: (no idea; something about lust i suppose)</div> </div> </div> </div>My first impulse is to suggest foods reputed as folk-aphrodisiacs like chocolate, oysters, softshell turtle, etc, but I wonder if that might be too on-the-nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T00:52:18-07:00","id":1523609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1518764-would-like-inspiration-and-advices-for-interesting-spirit-npcs?p=1523598#post1523598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Are you proud of yourself? Are you happy with what you have wrought? with the <i>sin</i> you have <i>committed here</i> in front of <i>witnesses</i>?<br /> <br /> If not, why aren't you, this was fucking hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my defense, I claim weakness of mind brought by a sharp lack of caffeine in my veins.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1518764-would-like-inspiration-and-advices-for-interesting-spirit-npcs?p=1523601#post1523601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first impulse is to suggest foods reputed as folk-aphrodisiacs like chocolate, oysters, softshell turtle, etc, but I wonder if that might be too on-the-nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The image of hitting a floating sandwich with chocolate is surreal enough that I'm taking it. (Though I won't edit it in above right now; i dont wanna risk angering the God-Machine's cold eyes atm)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T06:20:45-07:00","id":1523623,"title":"","content":"Would it have to be the meat of the turtle or oyster, or could you knap up a spearhead of the shells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236